{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ISA",
  "chapter": 43,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now thus saith the LORD that created thee, O Jacob, and he that formed thee, O Israel, Fear not: for I have redeemed thee, I have called ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by thy name; thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When thou passest through the waters, I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "will be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee; and through the rivers, they shall not overflow thee: when thou walkest through the fire, thou shalt not be burned; neither shall the flame kindle upon thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD thy God, the Holy One of Israel, thy Savior: I gave Egypt ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy ransom, Cush and Seba for thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Since thou hast been precious in my sight, thou hast been honorable, and I have loved thee: therefore will I give men for thee, and people for thy life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Fear not: for I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thee: I will bring thy seed from the east, and gather thee from the west;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will say to the north, Give up; and to the south, Keep not back: bring my sons from far, and my daughters from the ends of the earth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " every one that is called by my name: for I have created him for my glory, I have formed him; verily, I have made him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bring forth the blind people that have eyes, and the deaf that have ears.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let all the nations be collected, and let the people be assembled: who among them can declare this, and show us former things? let them bring forth their witnesses, that they may be justified: or let them hear, and say, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my witnesses, saith the LORD, and my servant whom I have chosen: that ye may know and believe me, and understand that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he: before me there was no god formed, neither shall there be after me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD; and besides me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no savior.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have declared, and have saved, and I have shown, when ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no strange ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "god",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among you: therefore ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my witnesses, saith the LORD, that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, before the day ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " none that can deliver out of my hand: I will work, and who shall hinder it?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD, your Redeemer, the Holy One of Israel; For your sake I have sent to Babylon, and have brought down all their nobles, and the Chaldeans, whose cry ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the ships.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD, your Holy One, the Creator of Israel, your King.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD, who maketh a way in the sea, and a path in the mighty waters;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who bringeth forth the chariot and horse, the army and the power; they shall lie down together, they shall not rise: they are extinct, they are quenched as tow.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember ye not the former things, neither consider the things of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, I will do a new thing; now it shall spring forth; shall ye not know it? I will even make a way in the wilderness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rivers in the desert.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The beast of the field shall honor me, the dragons and the owls: because I give waters in the wilderness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rivers in the desert, to give drink to my people, my chosen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This people have I formed for myself; they shall show forth my praise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou hast not called upon me, O Jacob; but thou hast been weary of me, O Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast not brought me the small cattle of thy burnt-offerings; neither hast thou honored me with thy sacrifices. I have not caused thee to serve with an offering, nor wearied thee with incense.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast bought me no sweet cane with money, neither hast thou filled me with the fat of thy sacrifices: but thou hast made me to serve with thy sins, thou hast wearied me with thy iniquities.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that blotteth out thy transgressions for my own sake, and will not remember thy sins.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Put me in remembrance: let us plead together: declare thou, that thou mayest be justified.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy first father hath sinned, and thy teachers have transgressed against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ISA.43.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ISA.43.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I have profaned the princes of the sanctuary, and have given Jacob to the curse, and Israel to reproaches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
